kdk patch 0001 (Wizarr v2026.10.1): refuse an existing LDAP user in create_user()

Upstream create_user() looks up the invitee's DN and, when it already exists,
calls _update_existing_user(), which replaces the entry's mail and resets its
password (RFC 3062) to what the invitee typed. Wizarr's service account must be
in lldap_admin to create users, so any valid invite code could reset any
directory password. This returns a refusal instead and leaves the entry alone;
_update_existing_user() stays in the file as dead code to keep the diff small.

Applied at image build by apply.py (zero fuzz: every context and removed line
must match exactly once, or the build fails). Path is relative to /app.

--- a/app/services/ldap/client.py
+++ b/app/services/ldap/client.py
@@ -205,7 +205,13 @@
             )
 
             if conn.entries:
-                return self._update_existing_user(conn, user_dn, email, password)
+                # kdk patch 0001: never modify an existing directory entry here.
+                # Upstream reset its mail + password to the invitee's input, so any
+                # invite code could take over any account (service account is admin).
+                logger.warning(
+                    "Refusing LDAP create: %s already exists (left unchanged)", user_dn
+                )
+                return False, "That username is already taken"
 
             return self._create_new_user(conn, user_dn, username, email, password)
 
